{"additions":1130,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds system-wide CPU / memory history graphs to the Procs page (issue spec: a new `graphs` pane), plus per-process CPU% / RSS sparklines in the detail pane. Read-only, numbers only.\n\nCloses #127\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`graphs` pane (\"System\")** — a full-width, 8-row pane above the existing panes:\n  - CPU: global CPU% history as a `Sparkline`, labelled with the current value and the recent peak; `c` (from the process list or the pane itself) toggles a per-core view with one small bar per core, laid out in columns.\n  - Memory: used-memory history scaled to the total, labelled `3.2G / 16.0G (20%)`; a swap line only when total swap > 0.\n  - Sparklines render right-to-left, so a buffer that is not full yet is right-aligned and grows leftward.\n- **Data** — the sysinfo snapshot now carries a `SystemSample` (global + per-core CPU%, used/total memory and swap). A pure `Ring<T>` buffer plus a `ProcHistory` map (per-pid CPU/RSS series, capped at the sample count and pruned to pids in the latest snapshot) live in `src/procs/domain/history.rs` with unit tests. Accumulation only happens while the page is active (ticks are per active page).\n- **Detail pane** — one-line CPU% and RSS history sparklines under the CPU / MEM fields for the selected process, dropped when the process disappears.\n- **Config** — top-level `procs-history \"<n>\"` (default 120, 10–10000), parsed/validated like `procs-refresh-interval`, replace-single merge; documented in `docs/config.md`.\n- **`VIG_PROCS_ROOT_PID`** keeps filtering the process list only — the graphs stay machine-wide by design (they contain no strings).\n- README / README.ja / config.md updated; `tape/demo-procs.tape` re-recorded with a graphs scene (sample accumulation, `c` toggle, detail sparklines).\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Linux rendering of the per-core grid (recorded and tested on macOS only; the code is platform-independent).\n- Behaviour on machines with very many cores (>32): the grid packs into columns but has not been seen on real hardware.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n\n## Update (2026-08-31)\n\nRedesigned the graphs btop-style after review feedback:\n\n- The one-line sparklines are now **filled multi-row area charts** (eighth-block columns) and every sample column is colored by load — green < 50 %, yellow ≥ 50 %, red ≥ 80 %.\n- Compact labels in the same gradient: `CPU  63%  peak 71%`, `MEM  29.2G/36.0G  81%`, and a `Swp` line when swap exists.\n- The `graphs` pane default height is 8 → 12 rows to give the charts room.\n- The per-core gauges and the detail pane's per-process CPU chart share the gradient; the RSS chart stays single-color (it is scaled to its own recent peak, where load colors would mislead).\n- The chart/color logic is centralized in `src/procs/panes/mod.rs` (`area_chart`, `load_style`) with unit tests; the demo GIF is re-recorded with a busy-worker detail scene.\n","changedFiles":17,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T02:55:19Z","deletions":45,"headRefName":"feat/procs-graphs","labels":[],"number":130,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcQTDw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are correctness/performance issues to address (quadratic PID pruning in `ProcHistory::record`, a tautological swap assertion in snapshot tests, and per-core grid formatting that breaks alignment on high-core-count machines).\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds CPU/memory history visualization to the Procs page, introducing a new system-wide “graphs” pane plus per-process CPU/RSS sparklines in the detail pane, with config support (`procs-history`) and updated docs/demo artifacts.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add a new Procs “System” graphs pane with CPU history/per-core toggle and memory(+swap) history.\n- Track per-process CPU% and RSS history and render sparklines in the Procs detail pane.\n- Add `procs-history` configuration (merge/validation/tests) and update docs + demo tape/GIF.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-procs.tape | Updates the Procs demo recording to exercise graphs + per-core toggle + detail sparklines. |\r\n| src/procs/state.rs | Wires in the graphs pane + history recording and routes the new toggle event. |\r\n| src/procs/panes/processes.rs | Adds `c` binding to toggle per-core CPU bars from the process list. |\r\n| src/procs/panes/mod.rs | Adds `spark_string` helper for right-aligned text sparklines. |\r\n| src/procs/panes/graphs.rs | Implements the new system graphs pane (CPU history/per-core grid, MEM(+swap) history). |\r\n| src/procs/panes/detail.rs | Renders per-process CPU% and RSS history sparklines under CPU/MEM fields. |\r\n| src/procs/domain/snapshot.rs | Extends sampling to include system CPU/mem/swap totals and per-core CPU%. |\r\n| src/procs/domain/mod.rs | Exposes the new `history` domain module. |\r\n| src/procs/domain/history.rs | Adds ring buffer + system sample + per-pid history structures with tests. |\r\n| src/core/pane.rs | Introduces a Procs-specific `ToggleCpuCores` pane event. |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Adds `procs-history` to replace-single merge rules and error messaging. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Implements `procs_history()` parsing/validation + tests and default-kdl expectations. |\r\n| README.md | Documents the new System graphs pane, the per-core toggle, and detail sparklines. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese documentation updates for the System graphs pane and keybindings. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Documents `procs-history` and updates Procs action lists to include `graphs`. |\r\n| assets/demo-procs.gif | Re-recorded demo GIF to reflect the updated Procs view. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds `procs-history`, adds `graphs` pane to Procs layout/tabs, and binds `c`. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T02:57:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"40cdb043ee91306a34f28c9c42f7f671e4333645"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLceUGw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:04:09Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"40cdb043ee91306a34f28c9c42f7f671e4333645"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLceUaQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:04:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"40cdb043ee91306a34f28c9c42f7f671e4333645"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLceUzg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:04:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"40cdb043ee91306a34f28c9c42f7f671e4333645"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcg_Gw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:16:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"55d9fa600d6daaf2296d3aa3a72491780f14fa36"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcg_eQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:16:25Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"55d9fa600d6daaf2296d3aa3a72491780f14fa36"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcg_7g","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:16:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"55d9fa600d6daaf2296d3aa3a72491780f14fa36"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLch0VA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe new rendering paths do avoidable per-frame cloning and potentially large per-frame allocations/scans that can become expensive with high `procs-history` values and/or many CPU cores.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**Previously missed (3)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/procs/panes/graphs.rs:283**\n* `render()` clones the latest `SystemSample` (`self.history.last().cloned()`), which clones the per-core CPU vector on every frame. This is avoidable work (and can be costly on high-core machines); borrow the last sample by reference instead.\n```\n        let Some(sample) = self.history.last().cloned() else {\n            f.render_widget(\n                Paragraph::new(Line::from(Span::styled(\"  Sampling...\", dim()))),\n                inner,\n            );\n```\n**src/procs/panes/detail.rs:187**\n* `DetailPane::lines()` allocates and converts the *entire* CPU/RSS history into a `Vec<f64>` on every render. With `procs-history` up to 10_000, this is a lot of per-frame work and allocation even though only `min(width, SPARK_W)` samples are displayed; truncate to the displayed window before building the temporary vectors (and compute RSS max over that same window).\n```\n        field(&mut out, \"CPU\", plain(format!(\"{:.1}%\", info.cpu)));\n        if data.cpu_history.len() >= 2 {\n            let vals: Vec<f64> = data.cpu_history.iter().map(|&v| f64::from(v)).collect();\n            continuation(\n                &mut out,\n```\n**src/procs/panes/graphs.rs:119**\n* `cpu_peak()` scans the entire history ring on every render. With `procs-history` up to 10_000, this makes rendering O(n) per frame and can become noticeably expensive; consider limiting the scan to a recent window (or caching the peak) so peak calculation stays bounded.\n```\n    /// Highest global CPU% in the buffer.\n    fn cpu_peak(&self) -> f32 {\n        self.history.iter().map(|s| s.cpu).fold(0.0, f32::max)\n    }\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:19:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"55d9fa600d6daaf2296d3aa3a72491780f14fa36"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcmqFA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nIt introduces cross-cutting UI/config/sampling changes (including platform-sensitive rendering paths) that warrant manual verification on multiple OSes and core-count scenarios.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:41:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"9ab769ff31543779622064e3dc088abc95327b53"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcpB_Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"9ab769ff31543779622064e3dc088abc95327b53"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcqHwA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nPer-core rendering can allocate/build far more grid lines than the pane can display on high-core machines, creating a avoidable per-frame performance/memory hit.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ddeb263567721c3c0d64f89acaefba24fb1f8406"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358612122/job/99385454703","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:51:48Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473822/job/99385061683","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:36Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:56Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473815/job/99385061359","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:36Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:51:33Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473822/job/99385061509","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:39Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:52:55Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473822/job/99385061673","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:37Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:52:55Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473822/job/99385424422","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:52:56Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358612122/job/99385472000","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:14Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:51:37Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473815/job/99385061470","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:36Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:51:40Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358473815/job/99385061507","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:50:37Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:07Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33358612122/job/99385478154","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:53:17Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Procs view: CPU / memory history graphs"}
